## Quick Reference: Building an Agent with Tools

```csharp
// 1. Define a skill class
public class MySkill : AgentClassSkill<MySkill>
{
    public override AgentSkillFrontmatter Frontmatter => 
        new("my-skill", "Performs useful tasks");

    protected override string Instructions => 
        "Use this skill to do something useful";

    [AgentSkillScript("convert-to-upper")]
    [Description("Converts text to uppercase")]
    private static string ToUpper(string text) => text.ToUpperInvariant();

    [AgentSkillResource("rules")]
    public string ReferenceRules => "Rule 1: Always be nice...";
}

// 2. Create agent
var client = new OpenAI.Client(...);
var agent = new ChatClientAgent(
    chatClient: client,
    instructions: "You are a helpful assistant",
    name: "MyAssistant",
    tools: new List<AITool> { ... });

// 3. Run agent
var session = new ChatClientAgentSession();
var response = await agent.RunAsync(
    "Hello, help me with something",
    session,
    new ChatClientAgentRunOptions(
        new ChatOptions { Temperature = 0.7f }),
    CancellationToken.None);

foreach (var message in response.Messages)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"{message.Role}: {message.Content}");
}
```

All classes and method signatures are exact from Microsoft.Agents.AI v1.13.0 and Microsoft.Extensions.AI v10.6.0.

